{"name":"Button Blue","hex":"#24a0ed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"button","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knob or disc that is passed through a loop or (buttonhole), serving as a fastener. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A mechanical device designed to be pressed with a finger in order to open or close an electric circuit or to activate a mechanism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten with a button.","To be fastened by a button or buttons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Button","blocks":[{"text":"A button is a fastener that joins two pieces of fabric together by slipping through a loop or by sliding through a buttonhole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Reserveknapper_til_Hans%27_uniform.jpg/330px-Reserveknapper_til_Hans%27_uniform.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Button","wikidata":"Q160464"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/500px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/1280px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/500px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern buttons made from vegetable ivory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_holes_buttons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg/500px-Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg/500px-Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spanish button (approx. 12 mm) from c. 1650–1675","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Doublet.jpg/500px-Doublet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Doublet.jpg/500px-Doublet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe